            <ArticleTitle>Exercise-induced hypoxia secondary to an atrial septal defect and cor triatriatum dexter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>793-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S1047951115001870</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 14-year-old boy presented to us with a diagnosis of severe asthma and oxygen desaturation of 76% on a 6-minute-walk test. A contrast echocardiogram revealed echocontrast in the left and right atria simultaneously. A secundum atrial septal defect and partial cor triatriatum dexter were diagnosed, and the atrial defect was closed by cardiac catheterisation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
